<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fiji</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fiji Islands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fiji is an island country in the south-western Pacific, made up of over 300 islands, chief among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viti-levu">Viti Levu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanua-levu">Vanua Levu</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suva">Suva</a>. Rival chiefdoms such as Bau dominated it until Seru Cakobau ceded the islands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1874. Indian indentured labourers brought to work on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations from 1879 formed a large community. Fiji became independent in 1970 and has since experienced several coups.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fiji.jpg" alt="Fiji" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tessa Mackenzie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Fiji.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
